yamlover/scalar
description: Atomic token — a YAML scalar or a pointer
- >
  An atomic token of yamlover is either any YAML scalar, or a **pointer** — and since a pointer
  dereferences to the node its path names, it stands wherever a value can. See the subchapters
  below for the two:
- *..:..:..:..:01-yaml:01-yaml_code:01-yaml_scalar
- *: 01-yamlover_pointer
